/* OmniCar – Split Screen – English */

"SPLITSCREEN" = "Split Screen";
"SPLITSCREEN_FOOTER" = "Two or three CarPlay apps side by side on the car screen, each with its real CarPlay interface. Changes apply right away. Turn off to use CarPlay as usual.";
"SPLITSCREEN_ENABLE" = "Enable Split Screen";

"SPLITSCREEN_ON_CONNECT_GROUP" = "In the car";
"SPLITSCREEN_AUTO_LAUNCH" = "Open split on connect";
"SPLITSCREEN_ON_CONNECT_FOOTER" = "When you connect, the most recent split reopens (or Favorite layout 1 if there is none). Layout, ratio and split direction (wide car screen: left/right, tall: top/bottom) follow the car screen; drag the bars between boxes to resize, remembered per app pair.";

"SPLITSCREEN_USAGE_GROUP" = "How to use";
"SPLITSCREEN_USAGE_FOOTER" = "Tap the Split Screen button on the CarPlay dock (just above Home) to show a panel with 3 sections: Default (2 boxes / 3 boxes / 1 large + 2: the open app goes to box 1, the other boxes show an app picker), Recent (the last 3 splits, tap to reopen the same apps and layout), Favorites (the layouts below). Holding an app icon for 1 second opens the same panel. While split, the button switches the layout (apps keep their box order; with fewer boxes the last apps go to the background). HyperOS style: drag the handle between boxes to resize (it snaps to 1/3 · 1/2 · 2/3), drag it to the edge to close the squeezed box, tap the handle for preset ratios, double-tap a divider to swap the two boxes. ••• bar on each box: tap for Replace app / Full screen / Close app; drag ••• onto another box to swap them. Closing an app removes its box (3 becomes 2, 2 becomes 1 = back to full screen). The CarPlay Home button closes the split.";

"SPLITSCREEN_PANEL_GROUP" = "Split Screen button panel";
